parable loss to the stakeholders. That means the balance of convenience and the irreparable loss coupled with the prima facie case are absolutely on the side of the petitioners and passing of interim orders in favour of the petitioners is extremely essential in order to protect the public interest and public estate which is intertwined with the estate of the Respondents. In this background of the matter, the Union of India has produced couple of judgments passed by the various authorities and Hon'ble Supreme Court, as stated below: In all these citations, it is very clear that there is ample power to invoke section 242 of the Companies Act, 2013 at any stage. In this background of the matter, we the Tribunal direct:

I.

That the Petitioner is permitted to serve the Respondents Through Joint Director working in office of post, publication in the newspapers, e-mail, WhatsApp messaging, wherever required, in order to ensure due service of notice to all Respondents present in India and overseas;

