u Section 406 makes provision for the application of sections 539 to 544, as modified and specified in Schedule XI to the Act, in the proceedings under sections 397 and 398. The said sections deal with offences by officers of a company for falsification of books, frauds, failure to keep proper accounts, fraudulent conduct of business and the power of the CLB 1/Tribunal to assess damages against such delinquent officers including the directors of a body corporate and partners of a firm if those are involved in the offences committed as well as imposition of penalties. Rules 11(a), 18 and 19 of the Companies (Court) Rules apply for the procedure. In Colaba Land and Mills Co. v. Vasant Corporation (1963) 2 Comp. LJ 89 (Guj.), it was mentioned that separate proceedings under section 406/543 (in Sch. XI) would have to be initiated against the persons found guilty of misfeasance, breach of trust or fraud in the course of proceedings under section 397/398. A contrary view was held in Life Insurance Corporation v. Haridas Mundra (1966) 2 Comp. LJ 371 (DB) (All.) that the Court may grant relief under the said sections with no separate application needed. It does not appear that the matters of imposition of penalties and assessment of damages dealt by Sch. XI came up for consideration by the Courts while dealing with the applications under section 397/398 in many cases reported. It is therefore unclear about the efficacy of Sch. XI in connection with applications for the prevention of oppression and mismanagement.

