Compulsory registration of intermediaries

18.16-2 Section 12 provides for the SEBI registration as compulsory for all intermediaries and prohibits them from carrying on any business otherwise than in accordance with the conditions of the certificate of registration issued by SEBI. Sections 30 and 29 empower SEBI to make and notify Regulations consistent with the SEBI Act, and for the Central Government to make and notify Rules. Application of other laws is not barred, section 32. [Regarding RTIs & STAs, see para 16.28]

