18.16-1e SEBI’s enquiry & directions - The important thing about these measures is that the opportunity of being heard, which it must be given to the alleged violators, either before or after such orders are issued by SEBI. If SEBI is satisfied after making or causing an enquiry that it is necessary, in the interest of investors or orderly development of securities market, or to prevent the affairs of any intermediary or other person associated with securities market being conducted in a manner detrimental to the interest of investors or securities market, or to secure the proper management of any such intermediary or person, it may issue directions to the intermediary or other person, and to any company in respect of matters specified in section 11A, as may be appropriate (section 11B).

18.16-1f Investigation by SEBI - If SEBI finds that reasonable ground exists to believe that the transactions in securities are being dealt with in a manner detrimental to the investors or the securities market, or any intermediary or other person associated with the securities market has violated any of the provisions of the SEBI Act/Rules/Regulations/directions issued by SEBI, it may order an Investigation of the affairs of the violator, to be carried out by the person, named in its order and to report on it. In the case of a company to be investigated in this behalf, it will be without prejudice to sections 235 to 241 of the Companies Act, and all officers and employees of the company or the intermediary or other person having the custody of all books, registers, other documents and record are duty bound to preserve and produce the same to the Investigator and answer his queries considered as relevant and necessary for purposes of the investigation by giving the requisite information or their explanations. If considered necessary, the Investigator may take and keep the books and papers in his custody for six months and return thereafter, subject to recall and grant of certified copies to the party if so required. The Investigator has been empowered to examine any person concerned with the affairs under investigation on oath the notes of which made by the Investigator have evidentiary value against the persons examined. For search and seizure of records suspected as being susceptible of being destroyed, mutilated, altered, falsified or secreted, and in the case of companies listed or to be listed where insider trading or market manipulation is indulged in, the Investigator has the power to do so, but before doing so he has to take out the order of the Judicial Magistrate of the first Class having jurisdiction (section 11C). SEBI has been vested with the power to order to cease and desist against the violation of the provisions of the Act done or caused by any person, and in the cases of companies listed or to be listed when SEBI has reasonable grounds to believe that insider trading or market manipulation is indulged in by such company, (section 11D).

